            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            We can further promote
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi fl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{fl}(Grp)
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            by taking the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi fl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Grp
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S[Grp] = Set^{C_{fl}(Grp)^{op}}  \, .
          %p
            By invoking
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*: S[Grp] \to E
            is the same as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h3#for_rings For rings
          %p The discussion above for groups can be repeated verbatim for rings, since they too are described by a finite products theory.
          %h3#ForLinearOrders For (inhabited) linear orders
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+sets"} cosimplicial sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta, Set]
              – hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              – is the classifying topos for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk95"}> Moerdijk 95, prop. 5.4
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For ease of notation we discuss this in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to PSh(\Delta^{op})
              are equivalently
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functors"} flat functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X : \Delta^{op} \to Set
            %p
              are equivalently linear orders. Evidently, such a functor is in particular a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              and we will show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              being flat is equivalent to this simplicial set being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              linear order regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-category"} (0,1)-category
            %p
              First assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              that exist in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              that exist in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              to limits in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo =
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi ⋯
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    [n] &amp; \simeq [k] \coprod_{[0]} [l] \;\;\;\; (n = k + l)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq [1] \coprod_{[0]} [1] \coprod_{[0]} \cdots \coprod_{[0]} [1]
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi l
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    X_n &amp; \simeq X_k \times_{X_0} X_l
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    X_1 \times_{X_0} \cdots \times_{X_0} X_1
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+space"} Segal relations
              that say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %p
              Moreover, since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              are characterized by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              being flat means that it sends jointly epimorphic families of morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              to monomorphisms in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\partial_0 : [0] \to [1], \partial_1 : [0] \to [1]\}
              is sent to an injection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (d_0, d_1) : X_1 \hookrightarrow X_0 \times X_0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              is the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              of the category that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the nerve of, this means that there is at most one morphism in this category from any one object to any other. Hence this category is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %p
              Finally to show that this poset is an inhabited linear order, we use the fact that a functor is flat precisely if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} cofiltered
            %p This means
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The category of elements is inhabited, hence the poset of which
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is the nerve is inhabited.
              %li
                %p
                  For every two elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y, z \in X_0
                  there exist morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %mi β
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta : [0] \to [k]
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in X_k
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi w
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\alpha) : w \mapsto y
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi β
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi w
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\beta) : w \mapsto z
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is the nerve of a poset, this means that there is a totally ordered set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ≤
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w  = (w_0 \leq  \cdots \leq w_k)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
                  are among its elements
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mrow
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = w_{\alpha(0)}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mrow
                              %mi β
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z = w_{\beta(0)}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \leq z
                  or
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \leq y
                  and hence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is in fact the nerve of a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y,z
                  are elements in the total order with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \leq z
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \leq y
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y,z) \in X_1
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z,y) \in X_1
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0(y,z) = d_1(z,y)
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi z
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_1(y,z) = d_1(z,y)
                %p
                  By co-filtering, there exists a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
                  over this diagram in the category of elements, hence morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %mi β
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta : [1] \to [k]
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in X_k
                  such that
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi α
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo :
                            %mi w
                            %mo ↦
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\alpha) : w \mapsto (y,z)
                      and
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi β
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo :
                              %mi w
                              %mo ↦
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi z
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\beta) : w \mapsto (z,y)
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi α
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi β
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_0 \circ \alpha = \partial_1 \circ \beta
                      and
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi α
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi β
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_1 \circ \alpha = \partial_0 \circ \beta
                %p
                  Here the last condition in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                  can only hold if
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo =
                          %mi β
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi const
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha = \beta = const_{i}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo =
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = z
            %p
              Conversely, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the nerve of a linear order. We show that then it is a flat functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \Delta^{op} \to Set
            %p (…)
          %h3#ForIntervals For intervals
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Andre Joyal
            showed that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{{\Delta}^{op}}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+intervals"} linear intervals
          %p
            Specifically a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{{\Delta}^{op}}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+interval"} linear interval
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+ordered+set"} totally ordered set
            with distinct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top"} top
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
            elements. In general, a linear interval is a model for the one-sorted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature"} signature
            consists of a binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            and two
            %span.newWikiWord
              constants
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/constant"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axioms
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash (x \leq x)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_y (x \leq y) \wedge (y \leq z) \vdash (x \leq z)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \leq y) \wedge (y \leq x) \vdash (x = y)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash (x \leq y) \vee (y \leq x)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash (0 \leq x) \wedge (x \leq 1)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi false
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0 = 1) \vdash false
          %p
            (Joyal calls this a
            %strong strict
            linear interval; by removing the hypothesis of distinct top and bottom, one arrives at a weaker notion he calls “linear interval”. Linear intervals in this sense are classified by the topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi a
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_{a}^{op}}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
          %p
            The generic such interval is
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1 \in Set^{{\Delta}^{op}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generic+interval"} generic interval
            for more details and references.
          %h3#for_abstract_circles For abstract circles
          %p
            The category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+sets"} cyclic sets
            is the classifying topos for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+circles"} abstract circles
            (
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk96"}> Moerdijk 96
            ).
          %h3#for_local_rings For local rings
          %h4#local_rings Local rings
          %p
            The classifying topos for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local rings
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/big+Zariski+topos"} big Zariski topos
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z})
            %strong local ring
            is a model of the geometric theory of commutative unital rings subject to the extra axioms
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi false
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0 = 1) \vdash false
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊢
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + y = 1 \vdash \exists_z (x z = 1) \vee \exists_z (y z = 1)
          %p
            In a topos of sheaves over a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalks
            are local. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topos"} locally ringed topos
            %a{:href => "#CoverPreservingFLatFunctors"} Cover-preserving flat functors
            below.
          %h4#StrictLocalRings Strict local rings
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topos"} étale topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X_{et})
            classifies “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+local+ring"}> strict local R-algebras
            ”. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} points of this topos
            are
            %em
              %span.newWikiWord
                strict Henselian R-algebras
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/strict+Henselian+ring"} ?
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hakim"}> Hakim, III.2-4
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#Wraith"}> Wraith
            ).
          %p
            See also
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/48690/what-does-an-etale-topos-classify"} this MO discussion
          %h3#PrincipalBund For principal bundles
          %p
            Essentially every topos may be regarded as a classifying topos for certain
            = succeed "s/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          %h4#BareGTor Over bare groups
          %p
            For any (bare / discrete)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            groupoid, the groupoid with a single object and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as its endomorphisms. The presheaf topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Set
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Set := PSh(\mathbf{B}G)
          %p
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
          %p
            For example, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            on (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set
            are the same as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Bund(X) \simeq Topos(Sh(X), G Set)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This follows via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X) \to Sh(\mathbf{B}G)
            are equivalent to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}G \to Sh(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Such a flat functor picks a single sheaf on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and encodes a
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a (bare, discrete) group, write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              for the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              the one-object groupoid version of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh(\mathbf{B}G)
                    \\to
                    Sh(\mathcal{B}G)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is a
              %em weak homotopy equivalence
              of toposes, in that it induces isomorphisms on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} geometric homotopy groups
              of the terminal object.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk95"}> Moerdijk 95, theorem 1.1, proven in chapter IV
            ).
          %h4#BareGTorGeomTheo In terms of geometric theories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            whose
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            = succeed "-torsors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:X\to X
            for every element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊤
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top\vdash_x \;1(x) = x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊤
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top\vdash_x \;g(h(x)) = (g h)(x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            into a
            = succeed "-set," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top \vdash\; \exists x \in X
            (inhabited-ness),
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x) = x \;\vdash_x \;\bot
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\neq 1
            (freeness), and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊤
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top\vdash_{x,y}\; \bigvee_{g\in G}\; g(x) = y
            (transitivity).
          %h4#TopGTor Over topological groups
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mo ×
                        %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\times \bullet}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(G^{\times \bullet})
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+on+a+simplicial+topological+space"} sheaves on this simplicial space
            is a topos.
          %p
            This is such that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a topological space, geometric morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X) \to Sh(G^{\times \bullet})
            classifies topological
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This idea admits generalizations to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+groups"} localic groups
            — and even to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+groupoids"} localic groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos+of+a+localic+groupoid"} classifying topos of a localic groupoid
            \.
          %h4#UniversalBundle
            The universal
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            At
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            it is discussed that the principal bundle classified by a morphims into a classifying object is its
            = succeed "," do
