                  }
                  \\,.
          %blockquote
            %p needs more discussion…
          %h3#ForLocalicGroupoids For general localic groupoids
          %p
            In fact,
            %em any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            can be thought of as a classifying topos for some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+groupoid"} localic groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+groupoid"} localic groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/10/geometric_representation_theor_2.html#c012724"} here
          %h3#for_flat_functors For flat functors
          %p
            As a special case of the above, any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functors"} flat functors
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (sometimes also called “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"}> torsor
            s”). In other words, geometric morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Set^{C^{op}}
            are the same as
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to E
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has finite limits, then a flat functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to E
            is the same as a functor that preserves finite limits.
          %h3#CoverPreservingFLatFunctors For geometric theories / cover-preserving flat functors on a site
          %p
            Another way, apart from that
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ForLocalicGroupoids"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            as a classifying topos is to start with a small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of definition for it. Any such site gives rise to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            called the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover-preserving+functor"} cover-preserving
            flat functors on that site (also called the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+flat+functors"} theory of J-continuous flat functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            Moreover, for any object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            which includes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is (part of) the universal object.
          %p We have:
          #EveryToposIsAClassifyingToposForLocalAlgebras.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+site"} cartesian site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, J)
              of definition.
            %p
              This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C}, J)
              is the classifying topos for cover-preserving
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              Every category of such functors is the category of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, remark D3.1.13
            ).
          %h3#LocalAlgebras For local algebras
          %p
            As a special case or rather re-interpretation of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CoverPreservingFLatFunctors"} above
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            be any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theory"} essentially algebraic theory
            and equip its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} syntactic category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{\mathbb{T}}
            with some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C}_{\mathbb{T}}, J)
            is the classifying topos for
            %em
              local
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕋
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            \:
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{O} : Sh(X) \to Sh(\mathcal{C}_{\mathbb{T}}, J)
          %p is
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕋
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+algebraic+theory"} algebra
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                of
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕋
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p such that this sheaf of algebras is local as seen by the respective topologies.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+algebra-ed+topos"} locally algebra-ed topos
            for more on this.
          %p
            By prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EveryToposIsAClassifyingToposForLocalAlgebras"}
            we have that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            is the classifying topos of
            %em some
            theory of local algebras.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            of this situation to the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            theory is the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} structured (∞,1)-topos
            and of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes%29"} geometry (for structured (∞,1)-toposes)
          %p
            The geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            that plays role of the syntactic theory. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{X}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            followed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{G} \stackrel{Y}{\to} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(\mathcal{G})
                  \\stackrel{\bar(-)}{\to} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(\mathcal{G})
          %p
            constitutes a model of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            in the (Cech)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(\mathcal{G})
            and exhibits it as the classifying topos for such models (geometries):
          %p
            This is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Structured+Spaces"} Structured Spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0905/0905.0459v1.pdf#page=26"} prop 1.4.2
          %h2#as_a_generalization_of_the_notion_of_classifying_space_in_topology As a generalization of the notion of classifying space in topology
          %p
            In view of the analogy between the classifying topos denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Bund(X)
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is equivalent to geometric morphims
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X) \to B G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Bund(X) \simeq Topos(Sh(X), B G)
                  \\,
          %p
            and the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B} G
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0 G Bund(X) \simeq \pi_0 Top(X, \mathcal{B}G)
                  \\,
          %p
            we should expect there to be a topos analog of the total space,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E G
            = succeed "," do
              %em generic G-torsor
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E G
            is that as a principal
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B} G
            = succeed "," do
              %em universal element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bdl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X, \mathcal{B}G) \to G Bdl(X)
            that it induces (by the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
            as the object representing the functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi G
                    %mi Bdl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto G Bdl(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C_T)
            of any geometric theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            comes with a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                generic
                = succeed "-model" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-model" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C_T)
            which represents the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi T
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \mapsto T Mod(E)
            in the same way. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            \= the theory of
            = succeed "-torsors," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-torsor." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
