          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Early references containing some remarks on the formation of the concept are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"}> Myles Tierney
                ,
                %em Forcing Topologies and Classifying Toposes
                , pp.211-219 in Heller, Tierney (eds.),
                %em Algebra, Topology and Category Theory
                , Academic Press New York 1976.
            %li#J77
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em Topos Theory
                , Academic Press New York 1977. (Also available as Dover reprint Mineola 2014)
          %p Standard textbook references for classifying topoi of theories
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                , Oxford UP 2002. (In particular, sections B4.2 pp.424-432, D3.2 pp.901-910)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Handbook of categorical algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p A more advanced reference containing several developments of the general theory, especially in relation with the view of toposes as ‘bridges’, is the monograph
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"}> Olivia Caramello
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/theories-sites-toposes-9780198758914"}
                  %em Theories, Sites, Toposes: Relating and studying mathematical theories through topos-theoretic ‘bridges’
          %p The relation between the existence of natural number objects and classifying toposes is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#blass
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Blass"}> Andreas Blass
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classifying topoi and the axiom of infinity
              %strong 26
              (1989) 341-345 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211840"}> doi:10.1007/BF01211840
              \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in relation to the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+infinity"} axiom of infinity
          %p The study of classifying spaces of topological categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classifying spaces and classifying topoi
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1616
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0094441"} doi:10.1007/BFb0094441
          %p The original theory for a general algebraic theory is developed in
          %ul
            %li
              M. Makkai, G. Reyes,
              = succeed "," do
                %em First-order categorical logic
          %p The results for the continuous groupoids include
          %ul
            %li#Moerdijk88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                , The classifying topos of a continuous groupoid I,
                %em Trans. A.M.S.
                %strong 310
                (1988), 629-668.
            %li#Moerdijk90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The classifying topos of a continuous groupoid II
                %strong 31
                no. 2 (1990), 137-168. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/numdam-bin/fitem?id=CTGDC_1990__31_2_137_0"}> web
                )
            %li#Moerdijk95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classifying spaces and classifying topoi
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1616
            %li#Moerdijk96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic sets as a classifying topos
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MoerdijkCyclic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Classifying toposes as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+algebra-ed+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} locally algebra-ed (infinity,1)-toposes
            are discussed in section 1.4 of
          %ul#Lurie
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Structured+Spaces"} Structured Spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topos"} étale topos
            as a classifying topos for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+local+rings"} strict local rings
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Hakim
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monique+Hakim"}> Monique Hakim
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topos annelés et schémas relatifs
            %li#Wraith
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Wraith"}> Gavin Wraith
              ,
              %em Generic Galois theory of local rings
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nikolai+Durov"} Nikolai Durov
            has introduced somewhat a generalization of topos called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vectoid"} vectoid
            and quite flexible notion of a classifying vectoid in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nikolai+Durov"}> Nikolai Durov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classifying vectoids and generalisations of operads
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.3114"} arxiv/1105.3114
          %h3#ReferencesRelationToForcing Relation to forcing
          %p
            Reviews of the interpretation of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
            as the passge to classifying toposes include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Blass"}> Andreas Blass
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+%C5%A0%C4%8Dedrov"} Andrej Ščedrov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classifying topoi and finite forcing
                %strong 28
                (1983) 111-140 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(83)90085-3"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(83)90085-3
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+%C5%A0%C4%8Dedrov"}> Andrej Ščedrov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Forcing and classifying topoi
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/memo-48-295/5"} AMS:memo-48-295
          %p For more see
          %ul
            %li#Roberts15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"}> David Roberts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Class forcing and topos theory
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/747/"} Topos at l’IHES
              2015 (
              %a{:href => "https://www.dropbox.com/s/vk1efw7lsvta80p/Roberts_IHES.pdf?dl=0"}> talk notes pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/4AaSySq8-GQ"} video recording
        .revisedby
